 panel.innerHTML=`<div class="eyebrow">03 · Assembly · operation ${number} of ${operations.reduce((n,a)=>n+a.length,0)}</div><div class="steps">${steps.map((s,i)=>`<button data-stage="${i+1}" class="${stage===i+1?'active':''}">${i+1} · ${s.shortTitle||['Thigh','Lower leg','Hip roll','Hip yaw'][i]||s.title}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="opprogress">${operations[stage-1].map((o,i)=>`<button data-operation="${i}" class="${operation===i?'active':''}">${i+1} · ${o.kind==='place'?'Place parts':'Fasten'}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="operation"><div class="optype">${op.kind==='place'?'PLACE PARTS':activeScrews().length?'INSTALL SCREWS':'RETAIN / CHECK'} · ${operation+1} / ${operations[stage-1].length}</div><h2>${op.title}</h2><p>${op.text}</p>${buildSection==='head-close'?'<div class="note amber">Complete the wiring stages and continuity checks before closing this cap. <button id="closure-wire">Open wiring guide</button></div>':''}</div><p class="intro">Place parts → fasten them → place the next parts → fasten again. Only parts introduced so far are shown; current parts stay solid, earlier parts are faded.</p>${motionPanel(op)}${op.retentionNotes?.length?`<div class="note">${op.retentionNotes.map(safe).join('<br>')}</div>`:''}${op.kind==='fasten'?`<div class="legend"><span><i class="dot" style="background:#1680be"></i>O · Output</span><span><i class="dot" style="background:#d47429"></i>C · Case</span><span><i class="dot" style="background:#8a53a1"></i>R · Rear center</span>${stage===2?'<span><i class="dot" style="background:#16836a"></i>F · Foot</span>':''}</div><p class="intro">${buildSection.includes('leg')?'Orange marks case screws, not orange printed screws. One motor ID can have several screw types.':'Each numbered marker matches one fastener below; mount fasteners are labeled M.'} Click a marker to see its fixing relationship.</p><div class="screw-list">${screwGroups(activeScrews())}</div><div id="screw-detail" class="note" aria-live="polite">Click a numbered marker or matching button to identify that exact screw.</div>${activeScrews().filter(c=>c.washer_mm||c.washerKey).map(c=>`<button data-washer-view="${c.id}">View ${c.servo_ids[0]?'ID'+c.servo_ids[0]:c.ownerLabel} washer stack</button>`).join('')}`:'<div class="note">Seat the shown parts first. The next operation identifies their exact screws.</div>'}${false?'<div class="note amber">Native dimensions: sleeve OD 14.6 mm, bore about 9.65 mm; lower-link boss about 10 mm; ankle pocket about 15 mm. The inner fit is already tight in CAD. Pressing it on can expand its outside, so nominal outer clearance does not prove a free real fit.</div><details><summary>Why keep this sleeve separate?</summary><p>A sleeve integrated into the lower link could still let the ankle rotate around its outer surface. A separate sleeve allows independent fit adjustment or replacement of a worn contact surface; these are engineering tradeoffs, not an explanation stated by the author. The ankle also has an axial retaining shoulder, so an integrated version would need an assembly-path check; simply merging these STLs does not establish that it can be installed. Current geometry is preserved. Check relative motion at sleeve outside ↔ orange ankle and its shoulder, not sleeve ↔ black link.</p></details>':''}<div class="row"><button id="previous" ${number===1?'disabled':''}>Previous operation</button><button id="next" ${number===operations.reduce((n,a)=>n+a.length,0)?'disabled':''}>Next operation</button><button id="fit-module">Focus this module</button></div><details><summary>Module check and fitting notes</summary><p>${st.check}</p><p>Mechanical alignment is separate from motor calibration. Leave output connections hand-snug for dry-fit; the pictured pose is not a calibrated motor zero.</p></details>${sourceFooter()}`;
