 panel.innerHTML=`<div class="eyebrow">Washer location · ${sid?'motor ID'+sid:safe(c.ownerLabel)}</div><h2>This thin silver ring is the washer</h2><p>The yellow highlight marks the <strong>metal washer</strong>. ${sid?'Its real size is Ø5 outside × Ø2.7 inside × 0.5 mm thick.':'Each M3 washer is Ø7 outside × Ø3.2 inside × 0.5 mm thick.'}</p><div class="stack-order"><span>1 · Screw head</span><b>↓</b><span class="washer-chip">2 · Metal washer · 0.5 mm</span><b>↓</b><span>3 · ${sid?'Black printed rear retainer':'Printed mounting faces'}</span><b>↓</b><span>4 · ${sid?'Motor rear-center hole':c.washerKeys?.length===2?'Opposite washer, then nut':'Retaining nut'}</span></div><p><strong>${sid?'ID'+sid:safe(c.ownerLabel)}: ${c.spec.replace(' x ',' × ')}</strong>. ${sid?'Slide the washer onto this screw before inserting it. The washer sits outside the printed shoulder, directly under the head.':c.washerKeys?.length===2?'One washer goes outside each hinge ear. The nut goes against the far washer; keep the tilt joint adjustable.':'The washer spreads the head load against the printed foot; the nut retains the other end.'}</p><div class="note">Parts are pulled apart along the screw axis to expose the stack. The screw shaft shows nominal size; its head and threads are simplified. Match the listed physical screw specification. The washer retains its actual dimensions.</div>${motionPanel({add:hardware})}<div class="row">${DATA.screws.filter(s=>s.washerKey||s.washer_mm).map(s=>`<button data-washer-jump="${s.id}">${s.servo_ids[0]?'ID'+s.servo_ids[0]:safe(s.ownerLabel)+' · '+screwCode.get(s.id)} washer</button>`).join('')}<button id="washer-return">Return to assembly step</button></div>`;
